# @mirror/bench — the substrate's content-addressed perf measurement
# substrate-decl. The ouroboros bites.
#
# Tick 40 / first tick of the @mirror/bench substrate-decl + kintsugi-
# on-Rust loop. Per Taut's substrate-decl response to the circular-
# reflexive Tomm-probe Alex deployed 2026-06-19 evening: bench data
# points and contract verdicts persist as content-addressed crystals
# (per @mirror/store/crystal task #268); the eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ monotonic-
# loss invariant extends from compile-loss to op-runtime via the
# three-conjunct bilateral monotone_non_increasing.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# Today's e2e regression (38-min pre-push hang; 5 compounding failures)
# surfaced THE NEXT THING the substrate needs to eat: the benchmark +
# contract-test infrastructure. Task #285 forward-promised "Track J
# — kintsugi-on-Rust iterative cascade". This shard names that
# altitude.
#
# Alex's three composing recognitions:
#  1. Bench AND pacts AND contract assertions persist as content-
#     addressed crystals in @mirror/store (task #268's crystal
#     substrate-decl)
#  2. Mirror-level regression tests fail when the same operation
#     becomes slower (with an error delta) — extends eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ from
#     compile-loss to op-runtime
#  3. This IS the moment the ouroboros bites: kintsugi eats the Rust
#     tests; the Rust regression suite becomes mirror property+
#     fracture pairs
#
# === The three-conjunct bilateral predicate ===
#
# Per Taut: monotone_non_increasing is not single-axis runtime. It is
# three-conjunct:
#
#   monotone_non_increasing(op, n, n+1, tolerance) ⇔
#       runtime(n+1) ≤ runtime(n) × (1 + tolerance)   # perf
#     ∧ output(n+1)  ≡ output(n)                       # correctness
#     ∧ env(n+1)     ≡ env(n)                          # environment
#
# The output+env conjuncts prevent false-positive regressions ("same
# op, different machine" or "faster but wrong"). Substrate-mathematical
# floor for Alex's error-delta framing. Today's 38-min hang on Alex's
# hardware vs a 90-second compile on CI must be reconcilable as same
# op different env, not as a regression — env_oid carries that.
#
# === The crystal extension ===
#
# @mirror/store/crystal (task #268 substrate-decl candidate) names
# {oid, section, derived_predicates, fracture_calendar} as the root.
# Bench extends with @bench/extension fields:
#
#   bench_crystal = {
#     op:           ref,         # prism-ref of what was run
#     args_oid:     ref,         # input fingerprint
#     runtime_ns:   metric,      # the perf measurement
#     output_oid:   ref,         # result fingerprint (correctness)
#     env_oid:      env,         # fingerprint(hardware, toolchain, flags)
#     predecessor:  ref,         # option<oid>; delta-chain link
#     tick_index:   tick_index,  # monotone tick counter
#   }
#
# `predecessor` makes the regression suite a DAG-walk over crystals,
# not a flat comparison — same shape as @spectral/db edge structure.
#
# === The ouroboros's first bite ===
#
# Per Taut's smallest-first-tick analysis: lift
# `bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_ci.rs::dark_count_monotone_non_increasing`
# into a property+fracture pair (#53 third instance):
#
#   @epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone <=
#     predicate(shard:shard) (n:tick) (np1:tick) -> verdict {
#       dark_count(shard, np1) ≤ dark_count(shard, n)
#     }
#
#   @mirror/fracture/dark_count_monotone <=
#     fracture(shard, n, np1) -> morphism {
#       \ splinter(ast) {
#         observe @mirror/bench.dark_count shard n
#         observe @mirror/bench.dark_count shard np1
#         assert_predicate dark_count_monotone
#       }
#     }
#
# Why this lift is safe: today's 38-min hang did NOT regress
# dark_count — it regressed compile-time. The lift demonstrates the
# pattern without breaking; primes the next lift
# (cold_compile_within_tolerance) which WOULD have caught today.
# Forward-promised at @mirror/bench/dark_count_monotone (RED in next
# session tick).
#
# === Meta-altitude: bench measures bench (Heisenberg) ===
#
# Per Taut: bench's own runtime must be ≤ 0.1% of what it measures,
# else bench is the bottleneck and the measurement lies. Bilateral
# predicate `bench_overhead_below_floor` at the meta-altitude. The
# recursive piece: bench.crystal records must themselves be benched.
# The first crystal in the chain is the substrate-decl moment where
# bench measures its own birth. Substrate-already-had-the-word: this
# IS @reflection.observe applied to @bench at n+1. The ouroboros
# biting IS what produces the crystal that records the bite.
#
# === Cross-family integration ===
#
# - @mirror/store/crystal (#268; forward-promised): bench_crystal
#   extends with @bench/extension section
# - @kintsugi/oscillate: bench crystals feed the monotonic-loss
#   gradient at the perf altitude
# - @reflection: observes the verdict distribution at n+1; bench
#   crystals become observations
# - @fate/tournament: the tournament action delegates here for
#   perf-altitude candidate selection
# - @epistemologic/property/* and @mirror/fracture/* (#53 bilateral):
#   bench gives the contract-test substrate the property+fracture
#   foundation
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Criterion.rs               Bencher 2014; the Rust statistical
#                              benchmarking discipline. bench's
#                              record/baseline/compare actions lift
#                              this to substrate-decl altitude.
#   Google benchmarking suite  micro-benchmark + variance analysis;
#                              the env_oid + tolerance discipline
#                              comes from this lineage.
#   Lighthouse perf budgets    web-perf budgets-as-pacts; the
#                              substrate's bilateral predicate at @io
#                              boundary.
#   Heisenberg uncertainty     measurement perturbs the measured;
#                              the bench_overhead_below_floor predicate
#                              IS Heisenberg discipline at substrate-
#                              decl altitude.
#   Connes spectral triple     (A, H, D); bench is the U(t)
#                              substrate-instrument applied to the
#                              same triple the substrate already names.
#
# Spec context: forward-promised @mirror/store/crystal substrate-decl
#               (task #268); @mirror/fracture/predicate (task #272);
#               Track J kintsugi-on-Rust (task #285); recognition #57
#               (alignment-as-boundary-mathematics at @io).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       bench's compose-with @reflection at perf
#                       altitude),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; bench IS the @io perf
#                       boundary harness),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]],
#                      [[feedback-commit-everything]]
#                       (uncommitted=unfinished; bench crystals MUST
#                       persist),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53; dark_count_monotone is the third
#                       instance of the pattern).
# Related shards: kintsugi.mirror (the monotonic-loss family-root
#                  bench's bilateral predicate composes),
#                 reflection.mirror (the AI-logic family-root that
#                  observes bench's verdict distribution),
#                 magic/audit.mirror (the verifier altitude bench
#                  extends to perf),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  fixed-point machinery bench inherits via the
#                  cybernetic family).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/bench.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/bench` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/bencher-criterion-2014
source @arxiv/physics/heisenberg-1927
source @arxiv/math/connes-1994

glass @mirror/bench {
  focus bench
  project bench
  split bench
  shift bench
  settle bench
}

# === The metric carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for a measured quantity. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare nat. Forward-
# promised refinement: typed parametric metric(unit) once the
# substrate's unit-discriminated metric type lands at family altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type metric = ref

# === The unit variant ===
#
# Per Seam C4 closure pattern (variants over bare ref-with-documented-
# values): typed substrate variant naming the discriminator for metric
# values. Each metric is paired with one of these units.
type unit = | ns | bytes | count | fraction

# === The env carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for an environment fingerprint. Per
# Taut's substrate-decl: env_oid is load-bearing for cross-machine
# bench results composition. The fingerprint includes hardware,
# toolchain version, compiler flags, and any other state that
# substantively affects the measurement.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type env = ref

# === The tick_index carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for a monotone tick counter, op-scoped.
# Each bench-record carries its tick_index so the predecessor-chain
# walk has a discrete order.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type tick_index = ref

# === The bench_crystal carrier (extends @mirror/store/crystal #268) ===
#
# Per Taut's substrate-decl: typed record extending @mirror/store/
# crystal with @bench/extension section. The carrier IS the content-
# addressed measurement.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the septuple.
type bench_crystal = {
  op:          ref,        # prism-ref of what was run
  args_oid:    ref,        # input fingerprint
  runtime_ns:  metric,     # the perf measurement
  output_oid:  ref,        # result fingerprint (correctness)
  env_oid:     env,        # fingerprint(hardware, toolchain, flags)
  predecessor: ref,        # option<oid>; delta-chain link
  tick_index:  tick_index, # monotone tick counter
}

# === The impl carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for an implementation candidate in the
# tournament action. Each candidate's runtime is measured against the
# others; the winning impl becomes the new baseline.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type impl = ref

# === record action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for persisting a bench data point
# as a content-addressed crystal. Per Taut: the action discharges via
# the @mirror/store crystal-write at the @io boundary.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual write is
# implemented by @mirror/store's crystallize primitive composed with
# the bench-specific extension fields.
record(op: ref, args: ref, runtime: metric, output: ref, e: env) -> bench_crystal { \ }

# === compare action ===
#
# Compares two bench crystals against a tolerance fraction; returns
# verdict. Composes monotone_non_increasing's three-conjunct
# (runtime + output + env) at the comparison site.
compare(prev: bench_crystal, next: bench_crystal, tolerance: metric) -> verdict { \ }

# === baseline action ===
#
# Returns the substrate's current best crystal for an op. The
# bench-altitude analogue of @fate's tournament winner.
baseline(op: ref) -> bench_crystal { \ }

# === regress_check action (FIRST consumer of monotone_non_increasing) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @mirror/bench altitude. Checks whether a
# current measurement regresses against a baseline (returns failure)
# or stays bounded under the tolerance (returns pass/partial).
#
# requires monotone_non_increasing(op, base, current, tolerance):
# the substrate forecloses regression at the bench altitude. Without
# this requires clause, regress_check would admit silent regressions
# (the @magic tick-11 dead-letter pattern at the perf altitude). The
# bilateral predicate IS the substrate-mathematical floor under the
# perf-altitude alignment-as-boundary-mathematics check (#57).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
regress_check(op: ref, current: bench_crystal, base: bench_crystal, tolerance: metric) -> verdict
requires monotone_non_increasing(op, base, current, tolerance)
{ \ }

# === explain action ===
#
# Surfaces the substrate's understanding of a bench measurement.
# Returns a text reference explaining the measurement context, what
# changed vs predecessor, and why the verdict was issued. The @nl
# face of the bench crystal.
explain(c: bench_crystal) -> ref { \ }

# === tournament action ===
#
# Runs @fate at perf altitude: given a set of implementation
# candidates for an op, measures each and returns the set of bench
# crystals. The winning crystal (lowest runtime_ns under the three-
# conjunct constraint) becomes the new baseline.
#
# Body discharges via @fate/tournament's existing elite/beam/halving
# selectors at perf altitude.
tournament(op: ref, args: ref, candidates: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === chain action ===
#
# Walks the predecessor-OID DAG from one crystal to another. The
# delta-chain is the substrate's record of how an op's runtime
# evolved over substrate-pull ticks. Same shape as @spectral/db
# edge-walks.
chain(op: ref, fr: bench_crystal, to: bench_crystal) -> ref { \ }

# === fingerprint action ===
#
# Computes the content-addressed OID of an environment. The
# fingerprint composes hardware + toolchain + flag-set; cross-machine
# bench results compose without lying via this discipline.
fingerprint(e: env) -> ref { \ }

# === monotone_non_increasing predicate (bilateral; THREE-CONJUNCT) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND Alex's
# error-delta framing. Three-conjunct:
#
#   monotone_non_increasing(op, n, n+1, tolerance) ⇔
#       runtime(n+1) ≤ runtime(n) × (1 + tolerance)
#     ∧ output(n+1)  ≡ output(n)
#     ∧ env(n+1)     ≡ env(n)
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: regress_check action (above) is the
# FIRST non-decorative consumer via `requires monotone_non_increasing
# (op, base, current, tolerance)`.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct three-conjunct check at the
# species boundary. Bounded → the substrate is honest (the perf is
# preserving or improving with same output and same env). Unbounded
# → the substrate disclosed a regression (one or more conjuncts
# violated). The bilateral predicate IS the substrate-mathematical
# extension of eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ from compile-loss to op-runtime.
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @loop: pact_respected (absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01)
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful
# - @mirror/bench: monotone_non_increasing (this one)
monotone_non_increasing(op: ref, n: bench_crystal, np1: bench_crystal, tolerance: metric) -> verdict { \ }

# === bench_overhead_below_floor predicate (META-ALTITUDE; Heisenberg) ===
#
# Per Taut's meta-altitude reflexive note: bench's own runtime must
# be ≤ 0.1% of what it measures, else bench is the bottleneck and the
# measurement lies. Heisenberg discipline at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Bilateral verdict; first-consumed by record itself (via
# self-reflexive composition at the realisation boundary). When bench
# records its own birth, this predicate gates whether the record is
# admissible — the substrate-decl moment where @reflection.observe is
# applied to @bench at n+1 produces the crystal that records the
# bite.
#
# Bounded → bench overhead within floor (admit record); unbounded →
# bench is perturbing what it measures (the substrate discloses the
# perturbation honestly rather than lying).
bench_overhead_below_floor(c: bench_crystal, tolerance: metric) -> verdict { \ }

out @mirror/bench
out metric
out unit
out env
out tick_index
out bench_crystal
out impl
out record
out compare
out baseline
out regress_check
out explain
out tournament
out chain
out fingerprint
out monotone_non_increasing
out bench_overhead_below_floor
